2026-09-23: TODO K02, bounded paired performance diagnosis; still OPEN.

Unchanged Images/config, fixed tcg-neoverse-n2-el2 contract, one vCPU in the
original demand_paging_test. Existing full runtime disks use snapshot=on.
Diagnostic arguments -m 3 -b 64M (one PA48/VA48/4K mode):
  GCC    1.487756000 seconds, original exit 0, TAP PASS, boot/shutdown PASS.
  EvoCC  5.220563008 seconds, original exit 0, TAP PASS, boot/shutdown PASS.
The original ten-mode 1 GiB/120-second failure is NOT closed by this reduction.

Profile fixture executes that installed binary without source modification,
using -m 3 -b 256K. GCC inlines user_mem_abort, so the common function-graph
root is kvm_handle_guest_abort, depth 6. All four trace buffers have zero
overrun/commit-overrun/dropped events; the fixture rejects empty/oversized logs.
Both reach 87 root invocations, 86 __kvm_faultin_pfn and stage2-map invocations.

Function (inclusive duration, microseconds)     GCC sum   EvoCC sum
kvm_handle_guest_abort                        41744.0    209663.0
__kvm_faultin_pfn                              14487.0     71637.9
kvm_pgtable_stage2_map                          9129.0     43530.1
kvm_release_page_dirty                         3600.9     17132.0
Instrumented guest execution: 0.066428000 / 0.304818992 seconds, exit 0 both.
These timings include instrumentation/scheduling and are not uninstrumented
performance claims. Sums are inclusive and must not be added together.
Call depth/inlining differs: a depth-limited leaf does not mean no child cost.
The measured excess is distributed across page acquisition/mapping/release,
not evidence of one deadlocked call or proof of a specific compiler defect.

Both profiles reuse the 64 MiB repair scratch disk and a 4.1 MiB initramfs.
Only the test, its libc/loader, the diagnostic and existing selftest-init are
included; no full runtime copy or new kernel build. No production code change.
Build with GCC 14.2.0-19, -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror in the sealed image.
Use existing gen_init_cpio and tools/k1/boot.sh; no alternate test framework.
K1_KERNEL_CONTRACT=contracts/kernel-selftest-kvm-target.json
